{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Who builds</b> — The reason to mention this: that He created the earth and all who dwell in it, and where can they hide and flee from before Him? And behold, in all the earth He touches, and it instantly falters — how much more so a mere fraction, the children of men who dwell in it, [being but] one among thousands of thousands. And He returned and said: for the earth cannot stand except by the power of the heavens, and the ma'lotot are the spheres of wind and cold and fire, for they are all spheres one above the other, and behold, these are between the earth and the heavens." "<b>And His agudah</b> — They are the living beings." "<b>Upon the earth He founded it</b> — that they are like bundles, and He mentioned another time: <b>who calls to the waters of the sea</b>, for the need of the living to bring down rain. And the meaning: that I prepared for the children of men all their needs, and behold, I will do good to them — if they obey My voice, and if they rebel against Me — they will not escape, for everything is in My hand."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:42.375070821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}